subsys/pmci/pldm: set the MCTP tag-owner bit on requester transmits

Fix the reverse-direction PLDM path (Zephyr requester EID 18 -> OpenBMC
responder EID 8). pldm_send_request_sync() transmitted requests with
MCTP_MESSAGE_TO_DST, i.e. tag-owner (TO) bit = 0 on the wire. A PLDM
requester owns the message tag (DSP0236 sec 8.1), so the request must be
sent with TO=1.

Why it only broke against the real BMC:

  * The BMC runs the Linux kernel AF_MCTP stack, not libmctp. Its input
    path (net/mctp/route.c mctp_route_input) only hands an inbound SOM
    frame to a bound listening socket when the frame has TO=1 and there
    is no matching existing key:

        if (!key && !msk && (tag & MCTP_HDR_FLAG_TO))
                msk = mctp_lookup_bind(net, skb);

    A TO=0 frame with no matching key is treated as an orphan response
    and dropped with -ENOENT before it ever reaches the PLDM responder
    socket. The mctp-serial line discipline still counts the frame in
    rx_packets, which is exactly the symptom we saw: rx_packets grew but
    the responder never received a datagram and tx_packets stayed 0.

  * The forward path (BMC requester -> Zephyr responder) always worked
    because Zephyr's responder replies with MCTP_MESSAGE_TO_SRC (TO=1),
    and the libmctp<->libmctp Type 0 loopback sample never exercises the
    kernel's TO gate, so the bug was invisible in unit tests.

With this change the Zephyr node's GetTID / GetPLDMTypes / GetPLDMVersion
probes to the BMC complete, the BMC base responder receives the inbound
requests (tag 0x08 == TO set) and answers them, and mctpserial0 shows
matching rx/tx counts. See docs/pldm-mctp-i3c-design.md sec 10c for the
end-to-end evidence.

Signed-off-by: HFM <hfm@example.com>

---

### subsys/pmci/pldm/pldm.c (modified)
diff --git a/subsys/pmci/pldm/pldm.c b/subsys/pmci/pldm/pldm.c
index 8fad0a7d856..20c196bcc9c 100644
--- a/subsys/pmci/pldm/pldm.c
+++ b/subsys/pmci/pldm/pldm.c
@@ -232,7 +232,16 @@ int pldm_send_request_sync(struct pldm_ctx *ctx, mctp_eid_t peer_eid,
 		memcpy(req->payload, req_body, req_len);
 	}
 
-	rc = mctp_message_tx(ctx->mctp, peer_eid, MCTP_MESSAGE_TO_DST, 0, tx,
+	/*
+	 * A PLDM requester owns the message tag (DSP0236 8.1), so the MCTP
+	 * tag-owner (TO) bit must be set on the wire. The Linux kernel MCTP
+	 * stack on the BMC only delivers an inbound SOM frame to a bound
+	 * listening socket when TO=1 (net/mctp/route.c mctp_route_input);
+	 * a TO=0 request is treated as an orphan response and dropped, which
+	 * is why the reverse-direction probe timed out despite the serial
+	 * layer counting rx_packets.
+	 */
+	rc = mctp_message_tx(ctx->mctp, peer_eid, MCTP_MESSAGE_TO_SRC, 0, tx,
 			     1U + sizeof(struct pldm_msg_hdr) + req_len);
 	if (rc != 0) {
 		LOG_WRN("mctp_message_tx failed: %d", rc);

